---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const schema = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'ProfilePage',mainEntity:{'@type':'Person',name:site.name,url:site.url+'/about/',jobTitle:'Product Owner',sameAs:[site.linkedin],worksFor:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Scheer IMC'}}};
---
<BaseLayout title="About & experience" section="About" schema={schema} description="Arslan Chaudhry, Product Owner at Scheer IMC. Enterprise platforms, technical product decisions and learner-facing AI.">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">About &amp; experience</p><h1>I want to understand<br />what makes it difficult.</h1><p class="lead">A customer request, a slow workflow or an impressive demo is a starting point. My work is to understand the system around it and help a team decide what to change.</p></header>
    <div class="about-layout">
      <aside class="about-facts"><p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p><dl><div><dt>Current role</dt><dd>Product Owner, Scheer IMC</dd></div><div><dt>Product</dt><dd>imc Learning Suite</dd></div><div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>Enterprise SaaS, platforms and AI</dd></div><div><dt>Opportunities</dt><dd>Senior PO / PM, remote or Berlin</dd></div></dl></aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Product work close to the system</h2><p>I work across platform modernisation and learner-facing AI at Scheer IMC. The problems are different, but they share a pattern: a product choice only makes sense when the technical and commercial constraints are visible.</p><p>That might mean recognising that a performance requirement calls for a different processing model. Or it might mean keeping two editors alive while customers migrate at different speeds.</p>
        <h2>How I contribute</h2><p>I frame the problem, write the conditions of satisfaction, connect work across teams and challenge assumptions before they become commitments. I work with engineering on technical choices and make my own responsibility explicit. Understanding implementation is useful because it changes the quality of the product decision.</p><p>The cases on this site include the cost of the chosen approach. Regressions, configuration drift and incomplete measurements matter. They explain what the next decision should take into account.</p>
        <h2>Selected experience</h2>
        <div class="experience-item"><p class="eyebrow">Jan 2024 to present</p><h3>Product Owner / Scheer IMC</h3><p>imc Learning Suite. Platform modernisation and learner-facing AI, including mass enrolment and the Page Editor migration.</p><a href="/work/">Read the cases</a></div>
        <div class="experience-item"><p class="eyebrow">Oct 2022 to Dec 2023</p><h3>Product Owner / PwC</h3><p>Product work involving document workflows, tagging and product demonstrations. This experience preceded my current focus on enterprise learning software.</p></div>
        <h2>What I am looking for</h2><p>Senior Product Owner and Product Manager roles in B2B SaaS where there is room to own a product problem, work closely with engineering and connect decisions to customer and business consequences.</p><p>If your product has difficult constraints, I would be interested to hear what they are.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Start a conversation <Arrow/></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
